Fix a SyTest harness crash: SyTest::Federation::Server::on_request_federation_v1_send
logs an "Unknown room" warning for any PDU whose room the mock federation
server's datastore does not know (a conforming homeserver may legitimately
deliver transactions for rooms the mock never joined or created). The
interpolation "${ $event->{room_id} }" is a bug under "use strict": it treats
the room_id string as a symbol name and dies with

    Can't use string ("!...") as a SCALAR ref while "strict refs" in use

killing the whole SyTest process and spuriously failing whichever test happens
to be running. Interpolate the value as a string instead.

--- a/lib/SyTest/Federation/Server.pm
+++ b/lib/SyTest/Federation/Server.pm
@@ -567,7 +567,7 @@
       if ( $room ) {
          my $event_id = $room->id_for_event( $event );
          $room->insert_event( $event );
       } else {
-         warn "Unknown room ${ $event->{room_id} }"
+         warn "Unknown room " . ( $event->{room_id} // "" )
       }
 
       next if $self->on_event( $event );
